  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity Building of the State Audit Office of Georgia (SAO)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Georgia):  Under the PASA the GAO/Center for Audit Excellence will assist the State Audit Office (SAO) in determining and estimating the potential effects associated with audit findings developed while conducting performance audits. While SAO has experience in conducting performance audits, it has not had significant experience in quantifying or estimating the potential or actual effects of its findings.This project will improve the quality of SAO&apos;s audit recommendations. The Program will introduce to SAO approaches and methodologies for quantifying and estimating potential or actual effects of its findings and will assist in developing policies and procedures for doing so.Program Objectives:Objective 1: Evaluate the current policies and practices of how SAO assesses the effects and impacts of performance audits and provide findings and recommendations on how to develop/improve them.Objective 2: Prepare the workplan (using the results of the evaluation) that will outline the specific capacity building tasks/activities that the Center of Audit Excellence will perform during the remainder of the project. Potential capacity building activities to be included in the workplan may include training, mentoring, and advisory tasks. As a result of the program, SAO will learn new approaches and methodologies for assessing and quantifying the effects of audit findings, that will improve the quality of audit recommendations, leading to increased number of recommendations implemented/resolved, and overall increase in effectiveness and impact of SAO audits.</narrative>
  </description>
